  "description": "# LSC-02 | Main | Hourly Luma Guests → SF Campaign Members\n\n**📋 Ticket:** [Luma guests → Salesforce campaign members](https://brightdata-group.monday.com/boards/8667788707/pulses/13343839880)\n\n---\n\n**TRIGGER:** Scheduler — every hour, Asia/Jerusalem\n\n**PURPOSE:** Sync queued Luma guests to Salesforce campaign members 1h after registration, retrying at 3h.\n\n**FLOW:**\n1. Get Pending rows with `next_attempt_at` ≤ now → PostgreSQL\n2. For each: call Fun 002 → write Done / Skipped / Not found / Error + SF IDs back to the row\n3. Not found on 1st attempt → stay Pending, retry in 2h; on 2nd → Not found\n4. New Not found rows → Slack field marketing (email, SF campaign name, member status)\n5. If new Error rows exist → mark notified and stop with error (→ System Error Handling)\n\n**DB / TABLES:** `marketing.luma_sf_campaign_queue` (read/write)\n**UPSTREAM:** LSC-01 | Fun 001 | Queue Luma Guest for SF Campaign Sync (fills the queue)  \n**DOWNSTREAM:** LSC-02 | Fun 002 | Sync Luma Guest to SF Campaign\n\n## Important logic\n- Attempts: +1h (Fun 001) and +3h (retry). Each Not found / Error row alerts once.\n- Slack channel: Marketing project property `lsc_field_marketing_channel`.\n- Max 500 rows per run; the rest are picked up next hour.\n",
  "name": "LSC-02 | Main | Hourly Luma Guests → SF Campaign Members",
  "private": false,
  "version": 3
